{"author":{"id":"596d9e1094c8ef9c6a292f8b8e62ea27e91d0fb3068244f343594b86d2cc5c1b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791063438,"nonce":"RFImc0dEEBGzG6Im520MOtkjjzs=","title":"The `/penny-drop/` page shell, end to end but without parsing. A Jekyll page with null layout and `/penny-drop/` permalink, following ADR 0001 (`penny-drop/docs/adr/0001-single-file-no-build-hand-rolled-tailwind.md`) and the site's get-down pattern (`get-down/index.html`): React 19 via esm.sh import map, JSX compiled in the browser, styling from the site's pre-built Tailwind 4 stylesheet (`/assets/index.css`). No JS build step.","message":"The page presents an iOS-styled canvas (`#F2F2F7` background, white card, SF system font stack) with a dashed iOS-style drop zone. The drop zone accepts drag-and-drop and also opens a file picker on click. While a file is dragged anywhere over the page, a full-window overlay appears so the user can drop without aiming. A privacy note states processing happens entirely in the browser. Dropping/selecting any CSV reads it into memory and shows a loaded state (e.g. file name) — no parsing yet.\n\nThe page is NOT added to the `/tools/` index; it ships quietly.\n\nDomain language per `penny-drop/CONTEXT.md`.\n\n\n- [ ] `/penny-drop/` serves a self-contained page (null layout, permalink), React via esm.sh, no build step\n- [ ] iOS canvas: `#F2F2F7` background, white card, SF system font stack\n- [ ] Dashed drop zone accepts drop and opens a file picker on click\n- [ ] Full-window drag overlay appears while dragging a file over the page\n- [ ] Privacy note: processing happens entirely in the browser\n- [ ] Dropping a CSV shows a loaded state with the file name\n- [ ] Page is not listed on the `/tools/` index\n\n\nNone - can start immediately","files":null}]}